    "result_text": "Build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the customerCode format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a single edit to one method in one file: `AssignCustomerCode.service`.\n\n- **CITY3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the owner's city\n- **LAST3** \u2014 first three of the last name (unchanged logic)\n- **NNNN** \u2014 now a per-city sequence: one more than the owners already in that city (filtering `findAll()` by `city`), instead of the old global count\n\nThe membership number (`OwnerMapper`) is derived from `getCustomerCode()` at mapping time, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 no change was needed there. That keeps structural impact minimal: one file touched, one small method changed, with no growth to the mapper class or the `Owner` model.",
